<title>UK: MasterCard to acquire control of Mondex - FT.</title>
<headline>MasterCard to acquire control of Mondex - FT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>MasterCard International, the credit card consortium, has agreed to acquire a majority stake in Mondex International, the Financial Times reported.</p>
<p>Mondex is the leading developer of plastic cards with memory chips that can be loaded with cash and used for small purchases.</p>
<p>The deal is expected to give MasterCard 51 percent of Mondex, which was set up by National Westminster and Midland of the United Kingdom but is now jointly owned by 17 banks, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, MasterCard would promote the Mondex electronic cash card through banks that carry its franchise.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
